{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5kMMC93ohSEMZC4R7MD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary of findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model at `Shipment.kt:9-13` with ShipmentStatus enum at line 23-27\n- Repository at `ShipmentRepository.kt` with `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()` methods\n- Controller at `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` with create/get/list endpoints\n- Error handling through ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) at `ApiExceptions.kt`\n- Error codes defined at `ApiError.kt:31-37` with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Controllers throw domain exceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError envelope\n- ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions and @SpringBootTest\n- All responses follow consistent error envelope with code, message, fields\n\n**Affected files to change:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - add confirm() endpoint method\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add tests for confirm scenarios\n3. `ApiError.kt` - add new error code for CANCELLED state rejection\n\n**Risks:** Breaking existing tests, incorrect idempotency handling, missing persistence, wrong status codes.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to distinguish CANCELLED rejection from other conflicts. This makes the error contract explicit for clients.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   This method:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CREATED, updates to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, saves unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - Returns OK (200) with the shipment body\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a service layer to encapsulate confirm logic: rejected because the controller directly uses the repository for create() and get(), maintaining consistency with existing patterns\n- Reusing VALIDATION_FAILED for CANCELLED case: rejected because it's semantically incorrect; CANCELLED is a legitimate state conflict, not a validation failure\n- Using a generic error code for all confirm failures: rejected because distinguishing state conflicts helps clients debug issues\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Status | Response |\n|------|------|-------|--------|----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById | save updated shipment | 200 | Updated shipment |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED | findById | save unchanged | 200 | Same shipment |\n| CANCELLED → error | findById | none | 409 | ApiError with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE |\n| Unknown ID | findById returns null | none | 404 | ApiError with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirm_moves_created_to_confirmed** — Create S-1 in CREATED, POST confirm, verify status is CONFIRMED in response and in repository\n2. **Test: confirm_idempotent_on_confirmed** — Create S-2, confirm it, confirm it again, verify second succeeds (200) with same response\n3. **Test: confirm_rejects_cancelled** — Create S-3, manually write CANCELLED to repository, POST confirm, verify 409 response with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n4. **Test: confirm_rejects_missing** — POST confirm on unknown shipment ID, verify 404 response with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the design. First, add the new error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":18227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86c5fae4-50ab-4f8a-9211-1915f504f96d","uuid":"d731bb0b-754d-47fe-b2aa-463ff231d024","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:06:29.487Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5kMLmapLKSbr3E3M1qa"}
